WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.733
That is a perfect way to sort them! You are looking at the actual geometry of the shapes rather than just their appearance.

00:00:06.733 --> 00:00:12.933
Ask your question out loud. Speak transcribes it and sends it for you.

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:20.467
Homework in another tab? Capture a screenshot, then ask about what you see.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:30.367
When you sort by two things at once, you are creating subgroups. For example, you could have a group for blue shapes and then split that into blue squares and blue non-squares.

